[2025-11-21 04:03:03] BUG FIX: Diff Base Selector Persistence

DESCRIPTION:
The diff base selector in the file explorer was failing to persist the selected commit, always reverting to HEAD.

CONVERSATION SUMMARY:
User reported that the selector never reflects the selected commit and diffs are not calculated against it.
Investigation revealed that the frontend function `changeDiffBase` was incorrectly calling `gitRequest`.
It was passing `fetch` options (method, body string) as the payload argument, causing the backend to receive a nested JSON object where the expected `ref` key was missing.
The backend defaulted to 'HEAD' as a result.

FIX DETAILS:
Modified `app/apps/file_editor_cm6/static/js/explorer.js`:
- Updated `changeDiffBase` to pass `{ ref }` directly to `gitRequest`.
- `gitRequest` handles the method and stringification internally when a body object is provided.

FILES MODIFIED:
- app/apps/file_editor_cm6/static/js/explorer.js
